# Build context exclusions.
#
# dashboard/static/ is deliberately NOT excluded: the built bundle is committed on purpose so
# the console runs with no build step, and the image ships it.
#
# dashboard/app IS excluded: it is the Vite source and its lockfile, which the image never copies
# and `package.json` "files" excludes from the published package for the same reason. Leaving it in
# the context would only slow the build down.
#
# Kept deliberately explicit. A broad pattern such as `*.md` would also drop bootstrap.md and
# event-schema.md, which the image needs (setup reads the shared policy source), so only the
# files known to be unnecessary are excluded here.
.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
dashboard/app
test
examples
CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md
CHANGELOG.md
THIRD_PARTY.md
README.md
LICENSE
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.gitignore
*.log
.env
.env.*
*.zstd
